		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5126&amp;p=37128#p37128"><![CDATA[
It appears to me that a lot of the questions raised on the forum regarding how to use the OpenGD77 firmware or the CPS are addressed in the User Guide.<br><br>I'm wondering if this maybe because the User Guide is not as prominently displayed as it could be, ie., at the moment to find it from the Board Index page you need to click on "FAQ", then "FAQ" again on the FAQs index and then scroll down to the "Is here a User Guide" question.<br><br>My thought is that if the User Guide was listed in the "OpenGD77 Information" section as a dedicated "User Guide" entry along with "Announcements" and "FAQs" it might make the documentation easier to find and allow people to locate the answers they are looking for.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4176">ZL2MGS</a> — Fri May 16, 2025 12:31 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
